Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-10-2001||10:49 AM||||I tried the Biggest Crane Compucam in my 2.8 and wasn't impressed at all.  Now it's time to buy a cam for my 3.1 stroker project and I want something AGGRESIVE damnit!  We've got the compression up to approx 9.3:1 and I want a healthy cam for it.  The car is setup with a 4.10 4sp, semi-race clutch(ACT kush-lok), extrude honed intake, larger TB, fuel mods, and fatter exhaust with a flowmaster(most of the mods thanks to 1FST2M6.)  So basically it's got a little extra flow, and I want a big cam to match it.  I've read somewhere that others have tried non-computer friendly cams with success, and I'm curious if any forum members have tried it.  The Big Crane Cam in my old auto GT made it pull a bit harder than other auto V6 Fieros in a race, but it wasn't really impressive.  Any ideas?  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||4
